  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Thursday) Issued at 1023 PM CST Thu \nNov 5 2026\n\nA cutoff low will gradually track into the Desert Southwest and \neventually northern Mexico by Saturday morning. Cloud cover will \nincrease Friday evening as mid-level moisture increases ahead of the \nlow. Leading shortwaves will reach the area early Saturday morning. \nECMWF continues a slightly more northerly QPF trajectory, however \nboth the GFS and the shiny new RRFS indicate a more southern track \nto the precipitation which has been favored given the best moisture \nand forcing is present there with the orientation of the low and \ndownstream flow pattern. Rain (mostly light) will track west to \neast through the morning across the southern South Plains and \nsouthern Rolling Plains and should be completely east of the area \nby evening. Currently totals look to be minimal. The \naforementioned upper low will gradually weaken and slowly track \nacross northern Mexico early next week. The associated \nprecipitation looks to remain over South Texas. Another weak upper\ndisturbance may bring rain chances late Wednesday into Thursday. \nIn any case, conditions look mostly dry beyond Saturday, with \nhighs increasing into the upper 60s to low 70s.",
